<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Monte Porzio</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1167">1167</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Tusculum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Monte Porzio was fought on 29 May 1167 near Tusculum, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, between the army of the Roman commune and imperial forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> under Archbishops Christian of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> and Rainald of Dassel, joined by Tusculan troops. The much larger Roman army was routed with heavy losses, opening the way for Barbarossa to take Rome that summer.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-monte-porzio.jpg" alt="Battle of Monte Porzio" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Luiclemens · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prataporci_site_Img_020.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
